Find the services that make a nominal chemical source usable (@cs-dependencies: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @chemical-supply-systems, #source "../sources/Chemical-Supply-Chains-and-Disruption-Risk-EPA.lingua#r_6Y999Z6S9P5T6FY75NA2HGVW6C", #source "../sources/Chemical-Supply-Resilience-EPA.lingua#r_2NVE96BRQ8Q3WYFP2ZQ3NTE11F", #source "../sources/Methanol-Safe-Handling-Manual.lingua#r_01VD6M07PMPE9J0W00Z9KD5WC0", #source "../sources/Oxygen-Pipeline-and-Piping-Systems-EIGA.lingua#r_7BBE969N5JQJES1KG9AKNBEZBV", #chemical-supply-systems "Maintenance-spares-qualification-and-return-to-service.lingua#r_7BWN32VFTEPBA8RYMSA5A1QRTQ") { r_3E7SBW7AQV33JYSRJ47ZCPDKED
**Read:** [Understanding Water Treatment Chemical Supply Chains and the Risk of Disruptions — EPA](../sources/Chemical-Supply-Chains-and-Disruption-Risk-EPA.lingua#r_6Y999Z6S9P5T6FY75NA2HGVW6C), the full report and disruption cases; [Supply Chain Resilience: Guide for Water and Wastewater Utilities — EPA](../sources/Chemical-Supply-Resilience-EPA.lingua#r_2NVE96BRQ8Q3WYFP2ZQ3NTE11F), the complete continuity guide; [Methanol Safe Handling Manual — Methanol Institute](../sources/Methanol-Safe-Handling-Manual.lingua#r_01VD6M07PMPE9J0W00Z9KD5WC0), the full asset integrity, contractor, training and operating-readiness sections; [Oxygen Pipeline and Piping Systems — EIGA Doc 13/20](../sources/Oxygen-Pipeline-and-Piping-Systems-EIGA.lingua#r_7BBE969N5JQJES1KG9AKNBEZBV), the complete operation/inspection discussion relevant to the case.

After the shared utility Record, draw the dependencies of a complete chemical delivery: electricity, water, heat/cooling, gases, communications, contact equipment, transport, measurement, maintenance and trained people. A supplier can hold enough chemical while lacking the functioning equipment or accepted evidence needed to deliver it to a user.

Choose one producer-to-user chain and identify each required service's location, capacity, operating state, replacement/repair needs and source of information. Include less visible work: calibration, laboratory reagents/reference materials, cleaning, inspection, package recovery, scheduling and technical review. Trace any dependency shared by both the main and backup route.

Develop an interruption scenario with a physical cause and chronology. Distinguish immediate loss of material from loss of the ability to maintain, measure or safely transfer it. Calculate the usable reserve against actual consumption and available delivery capability; a full reserve tank is insufficient if its required pump or vaporiser is unavailable. Use the EPA cases as concrete evidence and compare the proposed response with actual product/technical requirements. Later utility and machinery subjects supply their own full engineering depth while these interface Records show why they matter to chemical users.

**Continue:** [Maintain the ability to deliver accepted material over time](Maintenance-spares-qualification-and-return-to-service.lingua#r_7BWN32VFTEPBA8RYMSA5A1QRTQ).

